From c461c4e8a0e525d3bdfb5f3ffb96a875057e0cc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 17:16:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ship): gate auto-start PR shepherd watch on default-ON
 rail.auto_shepherd

`forge ship` already auto-starts the detached, self-stopping
`forge shepherd watch <pr>` monitor after a PR is created (watch.js +
watch-lifecycle.js + journal.js were all shipped in the Tier-1 work). The only
missing piece from epic c2d398e5 was making that auto-start honestly toggleable.

This registers a new default-ON, UNLOCKED runtime rail `rail.auto_shepherd` and
gates `maybeStartPrWatcher` on it: when a maintainer runs
`forge gate disable rail.auto_shepherd`, ship skips the watcher spawn; default-ON
behavior is unchanged. The rail check reads the SAME resolved runtime graph the
gate toggle writes (workflow.gates.rail.auto_shepherd.enabled), so it is
config-honest (#399), and it is FAIL-OPEN + wrapped so neither a disabled rail
nor a config-read error can ever fail ship (invariant preserved: never merges,
never resolves threads).

TDD: rail is registered default-ON/unlocked; autoShepherdRailEnabled is
fail-open (missing rail / throw -> enabled); maybeStartPrWatcher starts when
rail-on + PR, skips when rail-off, does not consult the rail on dryRun/no-PR,
and never throws into the ship path.

Refs cf8361bc, epic c2d398e5, 33e1bbd3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
